<section id="play">
  <div id="recording-sheet" class="hidden">
    <h2>Recording sheet</h2>
    <p>Enter the tree in the same order as the paper sheet, from the top downward: split feature, threshold, left prediction, then right prediction. Use a team name or first names only.</p>
    <p><label>Team name <input id="sheet-team" type="text" maxlength="80"></label></p>
    <p><label>Written confidence (%) <input id="written-confidence" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="1"></label></p>
    <div id="sheet-rows"></div>
    <button type="button" id="sheet-apply" onclick="applyRecordingSheet();">Apply tree and show the training score</button>
  </div>
  <div id="game-eval-band" class="game-eval-band">
    <div class="game-eval-results results">
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Player</th>
          <th>Confidence in model</th>
          <th style="width:240px;">&nbsp;</th>
          <th>Score<br/>(run 1)</th>
          <th>Score<br/>(run 2)</th>
          <th>Score<br/>(run 3)</th>
          <th>Score<br/>(run 4)</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You</td>
          <td id="confidence-user"></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;">% correctly classified (a)<br>Difference from confidence (b)<br>Score (a - b)</td>
          <td id="result1-user"></td>
          <td id="result2-user"></td>
          <td id="result3-user"></td>
          <td id="result4-user"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>vs Machine</td>
          <td id="confidence-stoopid-ai"></td>
          <td>&nbsp;</td>
          <td id="result1-stoopid-ai"></td>
          <td id="result2-stoopid-ai"></td>
          <td id="result3-stoopid-ai"></td>
          <td id="result4-stoopid-ai"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>vs Human+ML</td>
          <td id="confidence-hybrid"></td>
          <td>&nbsp;</td>
          <td id="result1-hybrid"></td>
          <td id="result2-hybrid"></td>
          <td id="result3-hybrid"></td>
          <td id="result4-hybrid"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Total</td>
          <td>&nbsp;</td>
          <td>&nbsp;</td>
          <td id="result1-score"></td>
          <td id="result2-score"></td>
          <td id="result3-score"></td>
          <td id="result4-score"></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <div class="expandable-box">
        <h1><strong>How evaluation works?</strong></h1>
        <span class="expand-button" onclick="toggleContent(this)">+</span>
        <div class="hidden-content">
          <p>Four sets of 20 cards are classified in four runs. In a class session those sets are fixed, so a re-run shows the same cards and the same scores. It does not add a new leaderboard row.</p>
          <p>When you click "Evaluate model," four sets of 20 cards, each containing unknown cities, will be selected and classified in four separate runs.</p>
          <h4><strong>1. Accuracy Against Your Confidence</strong></h4>
          <p>Your score is the percentage of correctly classified items minus the difference from your confidence.</p>
          <h4><strong>2. vs Machine</strong></h4>
          <p>The machine claims 100% because it memorised the 20 training cards. You win when your result is closer to your claim than the machine's is to 100%.</p>
          <h4><strong>3. vs Human+ML</strong></h4>
          <p>This opponent uses price per square foot and elevation. You win when you are closer to your claim than it is to its claim.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="game-eval-session-lb" aria-label="Session leaderboard">
      <h3>Session leaderboard</h3>
      <table id="session-leaderboard" class="display responsive wrap game-session-lb-table" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Rank</th>
            <th>Attempt</th>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Score</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="session-leaderboard-body"></tbody>
      </table>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
